<!-- Lyrics whose text starts with a verse number, as written by e.g. MuseScore: MusicXML has no element for the number.
  Measure 1, upper staff: verse 1 starts with "1. ", verse 2 with the wide (full-width) digit and period of Japanese text.
  Verse 3 starts a note later, with a short lyric, which is moved right like the other short lyrics (LyricsExtraXShiftForShortLyrics).
  The number is left of the lyric, which starts at its note like the lyrics of the other notes, and the notes are evenly spaced.
  Measure 2: "2. lah" in the upper staff is a later lyric of its verse, it starts with the number at the note.
  "1. lah" in the lower staff is the first lyric of the verse in that staff, with the number left of it. -->
